1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,480
Thin red text looks fuzzy and purple.

2
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:15,230
One red line. Three pixel formats.

3
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:25,660
1-pixel red line on blue. crf 0.

4
00:00:25,660 --> 00:00:37,590
Readers: decoded RGB, and chroma U and V.

5
00:00:37,590 --> 00:00:53,640
444: pure red. 422 and 420: purple.

6
00:00:53,640 --> 00:01:05,110
Neighbor pixel: 104, 0, 103.

7
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:12,980
422: horizontal line stays red.

8
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:20,860
420: smeared up and down.

9
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:25,530
Brightness at the line: unchanged.

10
00:01:25,530 --> 00:01:30,190
Color is lost, not light.

11
00:01:30,190 --> 00:01:35,490
420 shares color between pixels.

12
00:01:35,490 --> 00:01:42,920
Thin colored lines: 444, or accept it.
